WEBVTT

00:00:02.102 --> 00:00:03.433
Thank you.

00:00:04.504 --> 00:00:06.938
Oh, you look like a man
who could use more coffee.

00:00:06.973 --> 00:00:08.736
Keep it coming.

00:00:08.775 --> 00:00:11.300
I'm working
on my monthly ops report.

00:00:11.344 --> 00:00:13.642
So much has happened in the
last few weeks on this ship,

00:00:13.680 --> 00:00:15.238
I'm going to be up all night.

00:00:15.281 --> 00:00:17.806
This firenut blend
should keep your eyes open.

00:00:19.719 --> 00:00:22.415
Potent stuff.
Thanks.

00:00:23.456 --> 00:00:24.480
- Neelix.
- Yes.

00:00:24.524 --> 00:00:25.991
I know you have your
hands full this evening,

00:00:26.092 --> 00:00:26.990
but I could use your help.

00:00:27.093 --> 00:00:28.492
At your service, Commander.

00:00:28.528 --> 00:00:29.995
We're approaching
a class-1 nebula.

00:00:30.030 --> 00:00:32.498
Sensors are picking up traces
of protomatter inside.

00:00:32.532 --> 00:00:33.692
I understand you've
dealt with it before.

00:00:33.733 --> 00:00:36.293
Absolutely, when I was
making my living as a trader.

00:00:36.336 --> 00:00:38.395
Protomatter's one of the most
sought-after commodities.

00:00:38.438 --> 00:00:40.099
It's the best energy source
in the Quadrant.

00:00:40.140 --> 00:00:41.107
Well, we could use

00:00:41.141 --> 00:00:42.699
your expertise
in collecting a sample.

00:00:42.742 --> 00:00:43.709
We're leaving at 1400.

00:00:43.743 --> 00:00:45.005
See you in the shuttle bay?

00:00:45.045 --> 00:00:46.979
I'll be there, sir.

00:00:50.683 --> 00:00:52.981
These nutritional supplements
are unacceptable.

00:00:53.019 --> 00:00:54.145
What's wrong?

00:00:54.187 --> 00:00:55.984
They are pungent.

00:00:56.022 --> 00:00:58.217
That's the whole idea.

00:00:58.258 --> 00:01:00.590
I've been adding
Talaxian spices

00:01:00.627 --> 00:01:02.185
to broaden your palate.

00:01:02.228 --> 00:01:04.560
My palate is sufficiently broad.

00:01:04.597 --> 00:01:06.724
Why settle for "sufficient"?

00:01:06.766 --> 00:01:07.824
The Doctor tells me

00:01:07.867 --> 00:01:09.664
you have a full complement
of taste buds.

00:01:09.702 --> 00:01:11.101
You've hardly begun
to use them.

00:01:11.137 --> 00:01:13.537
Come by the Mess Hall
Thursday night.

00:01:13.573 --> 00:01:14.972
It's the first day of Prixin.

00:01:15.075 --> 00:01:17.441
We'll have an impressive array
of exotic cuisine.

00:01:17.477 --> 00:01:18.535
Prixin?

00:01:18.578 --> 00:01:20.637
The Talaxian celebration
of family.

00:01:20.680 --> 00:01:22.409
We observe it every year
on Voyager.

00:01:22.449 --> 00:01:23.916
Now that you're
part of the family...

00:01:23.950 --> 00:01:25.975
What should I do to prepare?

00:01:26.052 --> 00:01:27.178
Nothing.

00:01:27.220 --> 00:01:28.881
It's not a mission, Seven.

00:01:28.922 --> 00:01:30.219
It's a party!

00:01:30.256 --> 00:01:32.747
Ensign Wildman to Neelix.

00:01:32.792 --> 00:01:34.282
Uh, Neelix here.

00:01:34.327 --> 00:01:35.316
I hate to bother you,

00:01:35.361 --> 00:01:37.386
but Naomi's having trouble
getting to sleep again.

00:01:37.430 --> 00:01:38.522
Would you mind?

00:01:38.565 --> 00:01:40.590
No bother at all.
I'm on my way.

00:01:40.633 --> 00:01:43.796
If you'll excuse me,
duty calls.

00:01:43.837 --> 00:01:46.135
"Naomi"...I don't recall
that designation

00:01:46.172 --> 00:01:47.469
on the crew manifest.

00:01:47.507 --> 00:01:49.532
That's because she's not
a member of the crew.

00:01:49.576 --> 00:01:51.806
Naomi was the first child
born on Voyager.

00:01:51.845 --> 00:01:53.312
I'm her godfather

00:01:53.346 --> 00:01:55.814
and the only one that can
get her to sleep lately.

00:01:55.849 --> 00:01:56.838
Bon appetit.

00:02:03.123 --> 00:02:04.488
No monsters here.

00:02:04.524 --> 00:02:05.513
Good.

00:02:06.759 --> 00:02:08.750
Check the replicator.

00:02:12.665 --> 00:02:13.825
Ah.

00:02:13.867 --> 00:02:14.834
Nothing.

00:02:14.868 --> 00:02:17.268
Naomi, maybe Neelix
should check your room

00:02:17.303 --> 00:02:18.531
so you can go to bed.

00:02:18.571 --> 00:02:20.368
Okay.

00:02:20.406 --> 00:02:21.998
In there.

00:02:27.080 --> 00:02:28.945
Nobody here.

00:02:28.982 --> 00:02:31.007
There.

00:02:36.022 --> 00:02:38.889
Ah, there's not
a monster in sight.

00:02:38.925 --> 00:02:40.620
Can you stay longer?

00:02:40.660 --> 00:02:42.719
I'm afraid to go to sleep.

00:02:42.762 --> 00:02:44.423
Honey, Neelix has to go to work.

00:02:44.464 --> 00:02:46.125
Oh, it's all right.

00:02:46.166 --> 00:02:48.327
You know what I think about
when I'm afraid to go to sleep?

00:02:48.368 --> 00:02:50.302
No. What?

00:02:50.336 --> 00:02:53.669
The Great Forest.

00:02:53.706 --> 00:02:55.298
What's that?

00:02:55.341 --> 00:02:57.002
It's a place my people believe

00:02:57.043 --> 00:02:58.840
we're all going to go to
someday.

00:02:58.878 --> 00:03:02.905
It's a beautiful, beautiful
forest filled with sunlight

00:03:02.949 --> 00:03:05.645
and all the people who ever
loved me are gathered there

00:03:05.685 --> 00:03:08.449
to watch over me as I sleep,
to protect me.

00:03:08.488 --> 00:03:09.921
Really?

00:03:09.956 --> 00:03:13.414
Mm-hmm, and when I think about
that forest and those people,

00:03:13.459 --> 00:03:15.620
I'm not afraid to sleep anymore.

00:03:15.662 --> 00:03:18.961
Do you think those people
watch over me, too?

00:03:18.998 --> 00:03:20.966
I know they do.

00:03:21.034 --> 00:03:24.936
Now, I'm going to be away
for the next couple of days,

00:03:24.971 --> 00:03:27.531
so if you're afraid to sleep,

00:03:27.574 --> 00:03:29.940
I want you to think
of that Great Forest.

00:03:29.976 --> 00:03:31.102
All right.

00:03:31.144 --> 00:03:32.634
Pleasant dreams.

00:03:32.679 --> 00:03:33.976
Night, Neelix.

00:03:34.013 --> 00:03:35.071
Thank you.

00:03:44.190 --> 00:03:45.714
Cylinder...

00:03:50.430 --> 00:03:51.397
Oh!

00:03:51.431 --> 00:03:52.830
Sorry.

00:03:52.865 --> 00:03:55.993
I didn't realize you were home.

00:03:56.035 --> 00:03:57.002
I was regenerating.

00:03:57.036 --> 00:03:58.560
I see.

00:03:58.605 --> 00:04:00.869
Do you require assistance?

00:04:00.907 --> 00:04:02.670
No, no, no, I have a small

00:04:02.709 --> 00:04:04.870
containment cylinder
stored here.

00:04:04.911 --> 00:04:06.879
I'll just be a minute.

00:04:06.913 --> 00:04:08.574
Cylinder...

00:04:08.615 --> 00:04:11.709
Little cylinder, where are you?

00:04:11.751 --> 00:04:13.844
Cylinder, you were here
a month ago.

00:04:13.886 --> 00:04:15.751
Now, I know you
didn't just roll

00:04:15.788 --> 00:04:17.688
out of the airlock
all by yourself.

00:04:17.724 --> 00:04:20.056
Now, where are you?

00:04:20.093 --> 00:04:21.685
Oh...

00:04:21.728 --> 00:04:23.457
I'm sorry.

00:04:23.496 --> 00:04:24.463
I'm talking to myself.

00:04:24.497 --> 00:04:25.725
It's my way
of remembering things.

00:04:25.765 --> 00:04:27.926
You are a peculiar creature,
Neelix.

00:04:27.967 --> 00:04:29.161
Thanks.

00:04:29.202 --> 00:04:31.102
I think.

00:04:31.137 --> 00:04:32.468
Ah! Here it is.

00:04:32.505 --> 00:04:35.235
Oh, this will be perfect

00:04:35.275 --> 00:04:37.402
for containing
a small amount of protomatter.

00:04:37.443 --> 00:04:40.412
Last time I used
this little wonder,

00:04:40.446 --> 00:04:41.913
I nearly lost it to the Kazon.

00:04:41.948 --> 00:04:44.746
The Kazon... Species 329.

00:04:44.784 --> 00:04:46.149
You're familiar with them.

00:04:46.185 --> 00:04:47.550
The Borg encountered
a Kazon colony

00:04:47.587 --> 00:04:48.918
in the Gand sector.

00:04:48.955 --> 00:04:50.889
Grid 6920.

00:04:50.923 --> 00:04:53.448
Were they assimilated?

00:04:53.493 --> 00:04:55.427
Their biological and
technological distinctiveness

00:04:55.461 --> 00:04:56.758
was unremarkable.

00:04:56.796 --> 00:04:58.525
They were unworthy
of assimilation.

00:04:58.564 --> 00:05:01.089
I didn't realize the Borg
were so discriminating.

00:05:01.134 --> 00:05:02.431
Why assimilate a species

00:05:02.468 --> 00:05:04.368
that would detract
from perfection?

00:05:05.571 --> 00:05:07.038
Good point.

00:05:07.073 --> 00:05:12.670
Well, um, if you'll excuse me,
I'm needed in the shuttle bay.

00:05:12.712 --> 00:05:14.270
Pleasant...

00:05:14.314 --> 00:05:15.781
regenerating.

00:05:24.324 --> 00:05:26.121
One day a week...
that's all I ask.

00:05:26.159 --> 00:05:27.456
How hard can it be?

00:05:27.493 --> 00:05:28.460
Harder than you think.

00:05:28.494 --> 00:05:30.462
Neelix, it's pizza!

00:05:30.496 --> 00:05:32.726
Bread, tomatoes, cheese.

00:05:32.765 --> 00:05:34.562
The cheese alone
would take days.

00:05:34.600 --> 00:05:37.364
Separating curds and whey
from synthesized milk...

00:05:37.403 --> 00:05:38.427
it's a delicate process.

00:05:38.471 --> 00:05:39.961
So replicate the cheese!

00:05:40.006 --> 00:05:43.737
Since it means so much to you,
I'll see what I can do.

00:05:43.776 --> 00:05:44.765
Thanks.

00:05:46.412 --> 00:05:49.904
There's a concentration
of protomatter directly ahead.

00:05:49.949 --> 00:05:51.348
Neelix?

00:05:51.384 --> 00:05:53.614
Set the transporter
for 10,000 AMUs.

00:05:53.653 --> 00:05:55.086
Not a particle more.

00:05:55.121 --> 00:05:57.385
The containment field
is standing by.

00:05:57.423 --> 00:05:59.084
We're in range.

00:05:59.125 --> 00:06:00.456
Energizing.

00:06:07.967 --> 00:06:09.127
What happened?

00:06:09.168 --> 00:06:11.932
The transporter beam
ignited the protomatter.

00:06:12.004 --> 00:06:14.336
Shields are weakening.

00:06:14.374 --> 00:06:16.535
Disengage transport.

00:06:17.677 --> 00:06:19.201
Shields are down!

00:06:19.245 --> 00:06:21.270
I've got the sample, Commander,
and it's stable.

00:06:21.314 --> 00:06:22.474
Let's get out of...

00:06:31.023 --> 00:06:32.718
We're clear of the protomatter.

00:06:32.759 --> 00:06:34.283
How's Neelix?

00:06:38.564 --> 00:06:40.657
He's dead.

00:08:33.044 --> 00:08:34.841
No heartbeat.

00:08:34.879 --> 00:08:36.938
No synaptic response.

00:08:36.982 --> 00:08:38.847
Extensive cell damage
to his brain.

00:08:38.883 --> 00:08:40.373
Try a cortical stimulator.

00:08:41.286 --> 00:08:42.344
It won't work.

00:08:42.387 --> 00:08:44.947
His neural pathways were
disrupted by the protomatter.

00:08:45.023 --> 00:08:47.253
Set the stimulator
for an autonomic bypass.

00:08:47.292 --> 00:08:48.725
At least, we can get
his vitals going.

00:08:48.760 --> 00:08:49.886
It's too late for that.

00:08:49.928 --> 00:08:51.225
The damage was too severe.

00:08:51.262 --> 00:08:53.662
We're running
into more protomatter.

00:08:57.669 --> 00:08:58.693
I need your help.

00:09:09.080 --> 00:09:13.278
Captain's Log, Stardate 51449.2.

00:09:13.318 --> 00:09:16.287
After receiving a distress call
from Commander Chakotay,

00:09:16.321 --> 00:09:17.913
we've sent a beacon
into the nebula

00:09:18.023 --> 00:09:21.481
and we're in the process
of tracking down the away team.

00:09:21.526 --> 00:09:23.619
Captain, I'm detecting
a shuttle.

00:09:23.661 --> 00:09:25.151
Hail them.

00:09:25.196 --> 00:09:26.663
No response.

00:09:26.698 --> 00:09:28.723
The shuttle's primary
systems are off-line.

00:09:28.767 --> 00:09:30.928
Life signs, only two.

00:09:31.036 --> 00:09:32.435
Are they
within transporter range?

00:09:32.470 --> 00:09:33.437
Affirmative.

00:09:33.471 --> 00:09:34.529
Beam them directly to Sick Bay.

00:09:34.572 --> 00:09:35.937
Harry, put a tractor
on the shuttlecraft.

00:09:35.974 --> 00:09:37.441
Tuvok, you've got the Bridge.

00:09:40.578 --> 00:09:42.944
I ran a complete
postmortem analysis.

00:09:42.981 --> 00:09:45.950
There was nothing
you could have done.

00:09:45.984 --> 00:09:48.714
I knew we were too close
to the protomatter.

00:09:48.753 --> 00:09:50.118
I should have said something.

00:09:50.155 --> 00:09:52.521
Nobody could have
predicted this, Tom.

00:09:52.557 --> 00:09:54.218
How shall I...

00:09:54.259 --> 00:09:55.851
proceed?

00:09:56.961 --> 00:10:00.658
The Talaxians mourn their
dead for a full week

00:10:00.698 --> 00:10:03.360
in a specific burial ceremony.

00:10:05.503 --> 00:10:07.937
And that's just what
we're going to do.

00:10:07.972 --> 00:10:09.564
I'll inform the crew.

00:10:12.277 --> 00:10:14.074
I'll check Neelix's
personal data base...

00:10:14.112 --> 00:10:16.444
see what I can find out
about the ceremony.

00:10:16.481 --> 00:10:19.075
We'll have it in the Mess Hall.

00:10:19.117 --> 00:10:21.176
Somehow that feels
appropriate.

00:10:21.219 --> 00:10:23.119
Neelix is dead.

00:10:23.154 --> 00:10:24.644
I'm afraid so.

00:10:24.689 --> 00:10:27.317
His neural pathways...
are they intact?

00:10:27.358 --> 00:10:30.122
Yes, but there's
no metabolic activity.

00:10:30.161 --> 00:10:31.185
How long has he been dead?

00:10:31.229 --> 00:10:32.196
Seven, I understand...

00:10:32.230 --> 00:10:33.197
How long?

00:10:33.231 --> 00:10:34.255
It's been 18 hours.

00:10:34.299 --> 00:10:36.631
Then it's not too late
to reactivate him.

00:10:36.668 --> 00:10:37.635
What are you saying...

00:10:37.669 --> 00:10:39.569
that you can bring
Neelix back to life?

00:10:39.604 --> 00:10:41.128
That's precisely
what I'm saying.

00:10:42.140 --> 00:10:43.767
The Borg have
assimilated species

00:10:43.808 --> 00:10:46.003
with far greater medical
knowledge than your own.

00:10:46.044 --> 00:10:48.012
We are capable of
reactivating drones

00:10:48.046 --> 00:10:50.947
as much as 73 hours after
what you would call "death."

00:10:50.982 --> 00:10:52.813
Neelix wasn't a Borg drone.

00:10:52.851 --> 00:10:54.284
We will adapt.

00:10:54.319 --> 00:10:56.310
What does this "procedure"
involve?

00:10:56.354 --> 00:10:59.414
Nanoprobes are used
to reverse cellular necrosis,

00:10:59.457 --> 00:11:01.391
while the cerebral cortex
is stimulated

00:11:01.426 --> 00:11:03.087
with a neuroelectric
iso-pulse.

00:11:03.128 --> 00:11:04.595
But there's nothing
left to stimulate.

00:11:04.629 --> 00:11:05.755
His brain functions are gone.

00:11:05.797 --> 00:11:08.925
By your narrow definition
perhaps, but not by mine.

00:11:08.967 --> 00:11:11.800
You will extract 70 micrograms
of nanoprobes

00:11:11.836 --> 00:11:12.894
from my bloodstream.

00:11:12.937 --> 00:11:13.926
I will modify them

00:11:13.972 --> 00:11:16.497
to match
his Talaxian physiology.

00:11:16.541 --> 00:11:19.533
His function in this crew
is diverse.

00:11:19.577 --> 00:11:22.978
If you wish to salvage him,
we must proceed immediately.

00:11:23.047 --> 00:11:24.480
I say we let her try.

00:11:24.516 --> 00:11:26.643
Hold on a minute, Tom, please.

00:11:28.786 --> 00:11:32.950
No one's ever been resuscitated
after being dead for 18 hours.

00:11:32.991 --> 00:11:35.824
If this procedure does work,

00:11:35.860 --> 00:11:39.728
what are the chances that Neelix
would come out of it unaffected?

00:11:39.764 --> 00:11:40.822
She's right.

00:11:40.865 --> 00:11:42.924
The damage to his cerebral
cortex was severe.

00:11:42.967 --> 00:11:46.334
The nanoprobes will compensate
for any cellular degradation.

00:11:46.371 --> 00:11:50.330
Captain, a decision
has to be made quickly.

00:11:51.743 --> 00:11:53.802
Doctor, give Seven
whatever assistance she needs.

00:11:53.845 --> 00:11:54.812
Proceed.

00:11:54.846 --> 00:11:56.211
- Captain...
- Do it.

00:11:56.247 --> 00:11:58.340
If there's a chance
we can revive Neelix,

00:11:58.383 --> 00:11:59.509
we've got to take it.

00:12:00.585 --> 00:12:02.246
Keep me informed.

00:12:09.093 --> 00:12:11.857
The nanoprobes are ready.
We should begin.

00:12:11.896 --> 00:12:15.059
Hold on, I want to check
his blood viscosity.

00:12:15.099 --> 00:12:17.124
The cadaver has been
sufficiently prepared.

00:12:17.168 --> 00:12:19.693
And they say I have
a lousy bedside manner.

00:12:23.208 --> 00:12:26.700
Set neuroelectric iso-pulses
for one-second intervals.

00:12:31.549 --> 00:12:33.642
Ready.

00:12:33.685 --> 00:12:34.674
Now.

00:12:38.356 --> 00:12:40.847
Neural activity
at nine percent...

00:12:40.892 --> 00:12:42.382
10 percent...

00:12:42.427 --> 00:12:43.451
12 percent.

00:12:43.494 --> 00:12:45.121
This is incredible!

00:12:45.163 --> 00:12:46.596
His intracerebral
blood pressure,

00:12:46.631 --> 00:12:47.655
his synaptic responses...

00:12:47.699 --> 00:12:48.996
they're all returning
to normal.

00:12:49.100 --> 00:12:52.797
The alveoli in his lung
are regenerating.

00:12:52.837 --> 00:12:54.236
They should be functional...

00:12:55.273 --> 00:12:56.262
now.

00:12:58.343 --> 00:13:01.073
Neural activity at 52
percent and rising.

00:13:05.917 --> 00:13:08.750
His neurotransmitter levels
are rising too fast.

00:13:08.786 --> 00:13:10.276
We must stabilize
his motor neurons.

00:13:10.321 --> 00:13:12.414
I'm going to try reducing
his acetylcholine levels.

00:13:12.457 --> 00:13:13.424
It might be enough to...

00:13:13.458 --> 00:13:15.551
Doctor...

00:13:16.961 --> 00:13:19.327
Neelix.

00:13:19.364 --> 00:13:20.956
What... happened?

00:13:20.999 --> 00:13:22.432
What happened?

00:13:22.467 --> 00:13:23.934
Why am...

00:13:23.968 --> 00:13:25.401
why am I here?

00:13:38.782 --> 00:13:39.806
Dead.

00:13:39.850 --> 00:13:43.752
For 18 hours
49 minutes, 13 seconds.

00:13:43.787 --> 00:13:45.414
Congratulations, Mr. Neelix.

00:13:45.456 --> 00:13:47.390
You've just set
a new world record.

00:13:50.561 --> 00:13:52.358
That's impossible.

00:13:52.396 --> 00:13:54.159
You mean, I lost consciousness.

00:13:54.198 --> 00:13:55.631
I-I was, I was in a coma.

00:13:55.666 --> 00:13:56.826
No.

00:13:56.867 --> 00:13:57.959
You were dead.

00:14:01.805 --> 00:14:04.467
I'm stunned.
I'm amazed.

00:14:07.011 --> 00:14:08.672
I-I'm grateful.
Thank you, Doctor.

00:14:08.712 --> 00:14:10.612
Actually, you can
thank Seven of Nine.

00:14:10.648 --> 00:14:12.582
The procedure was her idea.

00:14:12.616 --> 00:14:13.947
Yours?

00:14:14.018 --> 00:14:16.885
The Borg assimilated the
technique from Species 149.

00:14:16.921 --> 00:14:18.081
I simply modified it.

00:14:18.122 --> 00:14:20.989
But you are welcome.

00:14:24.795 --> 00:14:26.490
Am I good as new?

00:14:26.530 --> 00:14:28.054
That remains to be seen.

00:14:28.098 --> 00:14:29.656
There's no way to tell
if your body

00:14:29.700 --> 00:14:31.395
will successfully
take over the functions

00:14:31.435 --> 00:14:32.925
the nanoprobes are serving.

00:14:32.970 --> 00:14:33.959
Nanoprobes?!

00:14:34.038 --> 00:14:37.439
It was necessary to repair
the necrotized tissue.

00:14:37.474 --> 00:14:39.169
Until I'm certain
the damaged tissue

00:14:39.209 --> 00:14:41.837
can function independently,
you'll have to be injected

00:14:41.879 --> 00:14:43.506
with nanoprobes
on a daily basis.

00:14:43.547 --> 00:14:48.143
Well, as long as I don't start,
uh, assimilating the crew

00:14:48.185 --> 00:14:49.709
or sprouting Borg implants...

00:14:49.753 --> 00:14:51.744
I'm sure I can live with it.

00:14:51.789 --> 00:14:53.450
I'm releasing you
to your quarters.

00:14:53.490 --> 00:14:55.219
Your body's
been through quite a shock

00:14:55.259 --> 00:14:56.351
so try to get some rest.

00:14:56.393 --> 00:14:57.826
Report to Sick Bay
tomorrow morning

00:14:57.861 --> 00:14:59.954
at 0800 hours
for your next injection.

00:15:09.340 --> 00:15:11.103
The shuttle mission...
was it a success?

00:15:11.141 --> 00:15:12.369
Did we get the protomatter?

00:15:12.409 --> 00:15:13.376
I'm afraid not.

00:15:13.410 --> 00:15:15.401
The sample you
collected destabilized

00:15:15.446 --> 00:15:17.073
before it got back to Voyager.

00:15:17.114 --> 00:15:20.447
The containment field needs
to be reinforced next time.

00:15:20.484 --> 00:15:21.644
If there is a next time.

00:15:21.685 --> 00:15:23.516
I've asked Chakotay
to find out exactly

00:15:23.554 --> 00:15:24.953
what caused the accident,

00:15:25.055 --> 00:15:26.682
and unless we can take
additional precautions,

00:15:26.724 --> 00:15:28.817
I'm not sending another
team into that nebula.

00:15:28.859 --> 00:15:30.121
I could help
with that investigation.

00:15:30.160 --> 00:15:31.286
No. You are taking
some time off

00:15:31.328 --> 00:15:32.295
and that's an order.

00:15:32.329 --> 00:15:33.318
No, Captain, please

00:15:33.364 --> 00:15:35.229
I don't need
any special treatment.

00:15:35.265 --> 00:15:38.530
Neelix, you've just
returned from the dead.

00:15:38.569 --> 00:15:40.696
Go easy on yourself.

00:15:40.738 --> 00:15:42.831
I suppose you're right.

00:15:42.873 --> 00:15:46.969
But you can't ask me to cancel
the first night of Prixin.

00:15:47.044 --> 00:15:48.375
The celebration
is in three days.

00:15:48.412 --> 00:15:49.777
Oh, I almost forgot.

00:15:49.813 --> 00:15:51.974
I've been aging fruit compote
in moolt nectar for weeks now.

00:15:52.049 --> 00:15:53.914
I-I can't just let it
go to waste.

00:15:53.951 --> 00:15:55.646
Only if you feel up to it.

00:15:55.686 --> 00:15:57.449
But could you not
ferment those compotes

00:15:57.488 --> 00:15:58.455
so long this time?

00:15:58.489 --> 00:16:00.514
Because last year, I got
a little light-headed.

00:16:00.557 --> 00:16:03.549
I'll make
the necessary adjustments.

00:16:03.594 --> 00:16:04.925
It's good to have you back.

00:16:04.962 --> 00:16:06.361
It's good to be back,
Captain.

00:16:34.625 --> 00:16:36.149
Alixia...

00:16:38.729 --> 00:16:40.458
why weren't you there?

00:16:45.736 --> 00:16:48.671
Human attitudes toward
death are perplexing.

00:16:48.705 --> 00:16:50.605
How so?

00:16:50.641 --> 00:16:52.541
Too much importance
is placed on it.

00:16:52.576 --> 00:16:55.409
There seem to be countless
rituals and cultural beliefs

00:16:55.446 --> 00:16:59.246
designed to alleviate their fear
of a simple, biological truth...

00:16:59.283 --> 00:17:01.683
all organisms eventually perish.

00:17:01.718 --> 00:17:05.586
I take it the Borg have no fear
of that biological truth.

00:17:05.622 --> 00:17:08.921
None. When a drone is damaged
beyond repair, it is discarded,

00:17:08.992 --> 00:17:10.926
but its memories
continue to exist

00:17:10.961 --> 00:17:12.895
in the collective consciousness.

00:17:12.930 --> 00:17:17.128
To use a human term,
the Borg are "immortal."

00:17:18.168 --> 00:17:20.295
You are no longer
part of the collective.

00:17:20.337 --> 00:17:22.737
You are mortal now,
like the rest of us.

00:17:22.773 --> 00:17:24.104
Does that disturb you?

00:17:26.577 --> 00:17:29.307
My connection to the Borg
has been severed,

00:17:29.346 --> 00:17:32.907
but the collective still
possesses my recollections,

00:17:32.950 --> 00:17:34.542
my experiences.

00:17:34.585 --> 00:17:37.713
In a sense, I will always exist.

00:17:37.754 --> 00:17:39.244
Fascinating.

00:17:39.289 --> 00:17:41.120
That must be a great relief.

00:17:41.158 --> 00:17:43.092
Yes.

00:17:43.127 --> 00:17:44.685
It is.

00:17:47.164 --> 00:17:49.291
I've sealed the fractures
in the shuttle nacelle.

00:17:49.333 --> 00:17:51.460
The rest of the repairs
should be completed by morning.

00:17:51.502 --> 00:17:52.833
Good.
How are you coming?

00:17:52.870 --> 00:17:55.498
I found a small phase variance
in the transporter logs.

00:17:55.539 --> 00:17:57.905
I think it was responsible
for igniting the protomatter.

00:17:57.941 --> 00:18:00.375
I've remodulated the transporter
beam to compensate.

00:18:00.410 --> 00:18:02.708
Good work.

00:18:02.746 --> 00:18:04.338
I'll be in Holodeck 2.

00:18:04.381 --> 00:18:06.281
I've created a simulation
of the shuttle accident

00:18:06.316 --> 00:18:08.181
to see if there's anything
we've overlooked.

00:18:11.054 --> 00:18:12.612
Commander.

00:18:12.656 --> 00:18:13.850
Commander, I thought
you might need

00:18:13.891 --> 00:18:14.915
some assistance on the holodeck.

00:18:14.992 --> 00:18:15.924
If you're feeling up to it.

00:18:15.993 --> 00:18:17.756
Well, I'm up to anything
at this point.

00:18:17.794 --> 00:18:19.591
I've been resting
for two days straight

00:18:19.630 --> 00:18:21.621
and resting makes me feel,
well, restless.

00:18:26.970 --> 00:18:28.267
I've programmed the simulation

00:18:28.305 --> 00:18:30.136
to start when we found
the protomatter.

00:18:30.174 --> 00:18:32.506
Why don't you monitor the
containment field readings?

00:18:32.543 --> 00:18:34.204
Gladly.

00:18:34.244 --> 00:18:36.109
Computer, display shuttle crew...

00:18:36.146 --> 00:18:38.410
excluding myself...
and begin program.

00:18:39.983 --> 00:18:44.215
There's a concentration
of protomatter directly ahead.

00:18:44.254 --> 00:18:46.654
Set the transporter
for 10,000 AMUs.

00:18:46.690 --> 00:18:47.952
Not a particle more.

00:18:48.058 --> 00:18:50.424
The containment field
is standing by.

00:18:50.460 --> 00:18:52.428
We're in range.

00:18:54.364 --> 00:18:57.231
The transporter beam
ignited the protomatter.

00:18:57.267 --> 00:18:58.734
Computer, freeze program.

00:18:58.769 --> 00:19:00.236
It looks like there
was a problem

00:19:00.270 --> 00:19:01.396
with the pattern buffer.

00:19:01.438 --> 00:19:03.133
It might have created
a feedback loop

00:19:03.173 --> 00:19:04.435
along the transporter beam.

00:19:04.474 --> 00:19:05.566
Sounds right.

00:19:05.609 --> 00:19:06.769
Let's keep an eye on it.

00:19:06.810 --> 00:19:08.903
See what happened
at the moment of impact.

00:19:08.979 --> 00:19:10.640
Computer, resume program.

00:19:13.217 --> 00:19:14.741
Shields are weakening.

00:19:15.786 --> 00:19:17.276
Shields are down!

00:19:17.321 --> 00:19:19.915
I've got the sample, Commander,
and it's stable.

00:19:20.023 --> 00:19:20.990
Let's get out of...

00:19:24.661 --> 00:19:26.788
Computer, freeze program.

00:19:38.375 --> 00:19:39.672
Nothing.

00:19:40.777 --> 00:19:42.608
What?

00:19:42.646 --> 00:19:47.447
I died, and there was nothing.

00:19:47.484 --> 00:19:50.578
There was no one there.

00:19:50.621 --> 00:19:52.589
No forest.

00:19:52.623 --> 00:19:54.591
Forest?

00:19:54.625 --> 00:19:57.856
The Great Forest.

00:19:57.894 --> 00:20:00.362
The afterlife.

00:20:00.397 --> 00:20:05.960
I was taught that when I died,
my ancestors would be there

00:20:06.069 --> 00:20:08.560
waiting for me
by the Guiding Tree.

00:20:10.240 --> 00:20:15.075
My sisters, my mother
and father, my cousins...

00:20:15.112 --> 00:20:18.104
everyone who was killed
in the war.

00:20:18.148 --> 00:20:21.515
I took great comfort

00:20:21.551 --> 00:20:25.749
in knowing that we'd all
be together again one day,

00:20:25.789 --> 00:20:28.724
but it's not true.

00:20:28.759 --> 00:20:31.159
Maybe we pulled you back
before any of that could happen.

00:20:31.194 --> 00:20:32.684
No.

00:20:32.729 --> 00:20:33.753
I was dead for 18 hours.

00:20:33.797 --> 00:20:34.786
I should have...

00:20:35.966 --> 00:20:36.990
experienced something.

00:20:37.067 --> 00:20:38.500
I should remember something!

00:20:42.673 --> 00:20:44.641
It's just a story.

00:20:44.675 --> 00:20:45.869
A myth.

00:20:47.044 --> 00:20:50.013
There is no Guiding Tree.

00:20:50.047 --> 00:20:52.845
No gathering of the ancestors.

00:20:52.883 --> 00:20:54.976
You can't be certain of that.

00:20:55.018 --> 00:20:56.645
Don't throw away
a lifetime of faith

00:20:56.687 --> 00:20:58.245
because
of one anomalous incident.

00:20:58.288 --> 00:21:01.951
Death is still the greatest
mystery there is.

00:21:02.059 --> 00:21:03.617
I was there.

00:21:03.660 --> 00:21:05.890
I experienced it.

00:21:05.929 --> 00:21:07.521
There was nothing.

00:21:10.267 --> 00:21:11.996
Computer, delete characters.

00:21:13.904 --> 00:21:16.236
That's what's going to happen
to all of us.

00:21:16.273 --> 00:21:19.674
Like a hologram...
we just disappear into nothing.

00:21:39.295 --> 00:21:42.355
Attention.
Attention.

00:21:42.398 --> 00:21:44.559
If I may have
everyone's attention.

00:21:47.703 --> 00:21:48.692
You might want to try

00:21:48.737 --> 00:21:50.398
the old "glass and spoon"
approach.

00:21:50.439 --> 00:21:51.599
"Glass and spoon"?

00:21:54.376 --> 00:21:55.468
Excuse me.

00:22:03.886 --> 00:22:05.217
Thank you.

00:22:06.522 --> 00:22:08.786
Welcome to the first
night of Prixin...

00:22:08.824 --> 00:22:11.952
the Talaxian observance
of familial allegiance.

00:22:11.994 --> 00:22:14.053
This year,
Mr. Neelix has requested

00:22:14.096 --> 00:22:15.961
that I commence the celebration

00:22:16.031 --> 00:22:17.896
with the traditional salutation.

00:22:19.401 --> 00:22:21.699
"We do not stand alone.

00:22:21.737 --> 00:22:23.967
"We are in the arms of family.

00:22:24.073 --> 00:22:26.337
"Father, mother,

00:22:26.375 --> 00:22:29.173
"sister, brother,

00:22:29.211 --> 00:22:30.769
"father's father,

00:22:30.813 --> 00:22:33.577
"father's mother,

00:22:33.615 --> 00:22:35.412
"father's brother,

00:22:35.451 --> 00:22:37.282
"mother's brother...

00:22:38.821 --> 00:22:40.686
fath..."

00:22:40.723 --> 00:22:43.954
Suffice to say,
the list is extensive.

00:22:43.992 --> 00:22:46.790
"We gather on this day
to extol the warmth and joy

00:22:46.829 --> 00:22:48.990
"of those unshakable bonds.

00:22:49.098 --> 00:22:52.226
"Without them, we could not
call ourselves complete.

00:22:52.267 --> 00:22:55.930
"On this day,
we are thankful to be together.

00:22:55.971 --> 00:22:58.439
We do not stand alone."

00:22:58.474 --> 00:22:59.441
Indeed, we do not.

00:22:59.475 --> 00:23:00.464
Here, here.

00:23:01.610 --> 00:23:05.706
A few days ago, we almost lost
a member of our family.

00:23:05.748 --> 00:23:07.272
I don't know how
the rest of you feel,

00:23:07.316 --> 00:23:09.147
but it scared
the hell out of me.

00:23:09.184 --> 00:23:10.617
Neelix,

00:23:10.652 --> 00:23:13.621
you still don't know
how to make a pizza...

00:23:14.656 --> 00:23:15.623
but I'm glad you're here.

00:23:15.657 --> 00:23:16.851
So am I.

00:23:16.892 --> 00:23:18.826
Here's to you, Neelix.

00:23:29.605 --> 00:23:30.970
Speech.

00:23:34.309 --> 00:23:35.537
Thank you, everyone.

00:23:37.346 --> 00:23:38.540
Well...

00:23:42.985 --> 00:23:44.748
enjoy.

00:23:44.787 --> 00:23:47.085
Computer, music.

00:23:54.530 --> 00:23:55.656
You all right?

00:23:55.697 --> 00:23:56.925
Fine, Commander, fine.

00:23:59.468 --> 00:24:02.460
I apologize for the other
day on the holodeck.

00:24:02.504 --> 00:24:05.064
I guess this whole "back
from the dead" thing

00:24:05.107 --> 00:24:06.438
is hard to get used to.

00:24:06.475 --> 00:24:08.102
I'm fine now.

00:24:08.143 --> 00:24:10.941
If you ever want to talk,
you know where to find me.

00:24:18.220 --> 00:24:19.710
Having fun?

00:24:19.755 --> 00:24:20.915
No.

00:24:20.956 --> 00:24:22.583
That's probably

00:24:22.624 --> 00:24:25.286
because you've been standing
here by yourself.

00:24:25.327 --> 00:24:27.090
I don't understand the rules
and procedures

00:24:27.129 --> 00:24:29.791
for this type of...
social occasion.

00:24:29.832 --> 00:24:31.163
The rules are simple.

00:24:31.200 --> 00:24:33.691
Choose a group of people.

00:24:33.735 --> 00:24:35.965
Listen to their conversation.

00:24:36.071 --> 00:24:37.299
Then when you feel

00:24:37.339 --> 00:24:40.331
like you have something
to contribute, chime in.

00:24:40.375 --> 00:24:42.070
"Chime in"?

00:24:42.110 --> 00:24:43.975
You say something.

00:24:44.012 --> 00:24:45.570
Join the discussion.

00:24:47.749 --> 00:24:49.876
I will try, Captain.

00:24:52.221 --> 00:24:54.553
The early stages
of Ktarian development

00:24:54.590 --> 00:24:55.989
are astounding.

00:24:56.024 --> 00:24:58.515
Naomi has grown five centimeters
since her last physical

00:24:58.560 --> 00:24:59.788
and that was
only three weeks ago.

00:24:59.828 --> 00:25:01.557
It seems like every time
I turn around,

00:25:01.597 --> 00:25:04.327
I'm recycling her clothes
back into the replicator.

00:25:04.366 --> 00:25:05.765
Children assimilated
by the Borg

00:25:05.801 --> 00:25:07.268
are placed
in maturation chambers

00:25:07.302 --> 00:25:08.929
for 17 cycles.

00:25:11.139 --> 00:25:13.130
Interesting.

00:25:13.175 --> 00:25:17.134
Well, if you'll excuse me,
I need to go talk to Neelix.

00:25:17.179 --> 00:25:20.512
In these maturation chambers,

00:25:20.549 --> 00:25:22.517
the development
of conversational skills

00:25:22.551 --> 00:25:25.884
is, I suppose, a low priority?

00:25:25.921 --> 00:25:27.149
Neelix.

00:25:27.189 --> 00:25:28.451
Oh!

00:25:28.490 --> 00:25:29.457
I'm sorry.

00:25:29.491 --> 00:25:30.822
No, no, no, it's all right.

00:25:30.859 --> 00:25:33.487
We haven't seen you
in a few days.

00:25:35.230 --> 00:25:37.221
I've been a little preoccupied.

00:25:37.266 --> 00:25:38.699
I understand.

00:25:38.734 --> 00:25:40.429
Naomi's been asking
about you.

00:25:40.469 --> 00:25:42.061
Really?

00:25:42.104 --> 00:25:44.504
She misses you,
and, frankly, so do I.

00:25:44.540 --> 00:25:46.804
She's had trouble sleeping
every night this week.

00:25:46.842 --> 00:25:48.469
"Only Neelix can tuck me in."

00:25:48.510 --> 00:25:49.477
"I want Neelix."

00:25:49.511 --> 00:25:52.071
It sounds familiar.

00:25:52.114 --> 00:25:54.344
Maybe you could stop by
later just to say hello.

00:25:54.383 --> 00:25:56.214
Why don't...

00:25:56.251 --> 00:25:57.650
why don't I go now?

00:25:57.686 --> 00:25:59.984
It's close to Naomi's bedtime.

00:26:00.088 --> 00:26:01.055
Are you sure?

00:26:01.089 --> 00:26:03.057
Prixin's your favorite holiday.

00:26:03.091 --> 00:26:05.116
Yes, but duty calls.

00:26:08.864 --> 00:26:11.230
Attention, all monsters.

00:26:11.266 --> 00:26:13.029
Get out of this room!

00:26:13.068 --> 00:26:14.899
My bed!

00:26:14.937 --> 00:26:17.462
Oh, there's no monsters here.

00:26:19.408 --> 00:26:20.375
It's a monster!

00:26:20.409 --> 00:26:22.172
Scared you!

00:26:22.210 --> 00:26:24.110
You certainly did.

00:26:24.146 --> 00:26:26.341
Pleasant dreams, sweeting.

00:26:26.381 --> 00:26:28.941
Can you stay longer?

00:26:29.051 --> 00:26:31.952
I want to hear
about the Great Forest again.

00:26:32.020 --> 00:26:33.612
The Great Forest?

00:26:33.655 --> 00:26:34.952
The special place.

00:26:34.990 --> 00:26:37.584
The place you think about
when you can't sleep.

00:26:39.962 --> 00:26:41.589
Are you sure you want
to hear about that?

00:26:41.630 --> 00:26:42.790
It's just a silly old story.

00:26:42.831 --> 00:26:44.298
Please.

00:26:47.035 --> 00:26:48.400
Well...

00:26:51.340 --> 00:26:53.501
it's a beautiful place,

00:26:53.542 --> 00:26:55.669
filled with sunlight...

00:26:55.711 --> 00:26:58.771
And all the people
who ever loved me.

00:27:00.549 --> 00:27:03.211
Yes.
They've all gathered there...

00:27:04.820 --> 00:27:08.256
to watch over you,
to protect you while you sleep.

00:27:08.290 --> 00:27:12.056
I had a dream about
the Great Forest last night.

00:27:12.094 --> 00:27:14.358
You did?

00:27:14.396 --> 00:27:16.830
There was trees,

00:27:16.865 --> 00:27:18.093
and grass,

00:27:18.133 --> 00:27:19.725
and animals.

00:27:19.768 --> 00:27:21.360
And I saw you and Mommy

00:27:21.403 --> 00:27:22.961
and we were all happy.

00:27:24.773 --> 00:27:26.570
Sounds like a nice dream.

00:27:26.608 --> 00:27:28.838
It was beautiful.

00:27:41.423 --> 00:27:43.948
The Doctor asked me
to run a hematological scan.

00:27:44.026 --> 00:27:45.493
Why?

00:27:45.527 --> 00:27:46.858
To regulate the dosage
of nanoprobes

00:27:46.895 --> 00:27:48.260
for your next injection.

00:27:54.936 --> 00:27:55.994
Go ahead.

00:27:58.507 --> 00:28:01.305
How much longer will I
be needing these injections?

00:28:01.343 --> 00:28:03.834
Until your damaged cells
can function on their own.

00:28:06.081 --> 00:28:08.879
I don't really like the
idea of Borg technology

00:28:08.917 --> 00:28:11.078
swimming around inside me.

00:28:11.119 --> 00:28:12.279
That is irrelevant.

00:28:12.320 --> 00:28:14.254
You need the nanoprobes
to live.

00:28:14.289 --> 00:28:15.483
"Live"?

00:28:15.524 --> 00:28:18.391
Oh, is that what I am
doing right now, living?

00:28:18.427 --> 00:28:20.918
I'm beginning to wonder.

00:28:20.962 --> 00:28:22.896
By most definitions,
you are alive.

00:28:22.931 --> 00:28:25.297
Well, part of me isn't alive.

00:28:25.333 --> 00:28:27.130
Which part
are you referring to?

00:28:27.169 --> 00:28:29.103
I don't know,
but something is missing.

00:28:29.137 --> 00:28:31.332
I don't feel
like Neelix anymore.

00:28:31.373 --> 00:28:34.137
Maybe Neelix is gone.

00:28:34.176 --> 00:28:36.542
Maybe he died
and I'm all that's left.

00:28:36.578 --> 00:28:39.069
Stop moving and allow me
to complete the scan.

00:28:39.114 --> 00:28:42.208
I-I didn't ask
to be brought back!

00:28:42.250 --> 00:28:43.649
You were dead at the time.

00:28:43.685 --> 00:28:45.846
Well, what right did you have
to violate me?

00:28:45.887 --> 00:28:47.320
You Borg think
you can fix anything,

00:28:47.355 --> 00:28:48.913
but you didn't fix me!

00:28:48.957 --> 00:28:50.447
There was no alternative.

00:28:50.492 --> 00:28:51.720
Just get out.

00:28:51.760 --> 00:28:53.728
Just leave me alone!

00:28:53.762 --> 00:28:54.956
I said get out!

00:28:55.030 --> 00:28:57.555
I would be negligent in
my duties if I did that.

00:28:57.599 --> 00:28:58.657
I don't care about your duties!

00:28:58.700 --> 00:28:59.689
I don't care...

00:29:11.646 --> 00:29:13.614
What's...

00:29:13.648 --> 00:29:14.945
what's happening to me?

00:29:16.318 --> 00:29:18.582
Your cells are reverting
to a necrotic state.

00:29:18.620 --> 00:29:19.848
We must get you to Sick Bay.

00:29:24.825 --> 00:29:26.793
His tissue began
rejecting the nanoprobes,

00:29:26.827 --> 00:29:29.489
causing spontaneous necrosis
throughout his body.

00:29:29.530 --> 00:29:31.555
We modified the nanoprobes
to compensate

00:29:31.599 --> 00:29:33.089
and it appears to be working...

00:29:33.133 --> 00:29:35.192
Neelix is stable...
for now.

00:29:35.235 --> 00:29:36.759
How do we know this
won't happen again?

00:29:36.804 --> 00:29:39.637
We don't. I've designed
a monitor for Neelix to wear

00:29:39.673 --> 00:29:41.800
that will alert us
at the first sign of necrosis

00:29:41.842 --> 00:29:43.833
and we'll continue
with the daily injections.

00:29:43.877 --> 00:29:46.937
Beyond that, I'm afraid
it's a...

00:29:46.981 --> 00:29:48.380
matter of maintenance.

00:29:48.415 --> 00:29:49.939
He may have to live
with this condition

00:29:50.017 --> 00:29:51.075
for the rest of his life.

00:29:51.118 --> 00:29:53.018
He wants to speak
with you, Commander.

00:29:58.626 --> 00:30:03.063
Commander... you said
if I ever needed anything.

00:30:03.097 --> 00:30:06.498
You once told me
your people had technology

00:30:06.533 --> 00:30:08.398
that can induce
a deep meditation...

00:30:08.435 --> 00:30:10.460
an altered state
of consciousness.

00:30:10.504 --> 00:30:11.732
The akoonah.

00:30:11.772 --> 00:30:14.969
That this device allows you
to look inside yourself,

00:30:15.042 --> 00:30:19.979
ask questions that you might
otherwise be afraid to ask.

00:30:20.047 --> 00:30:20.979
That's right.

00:30:21.081 --> 00:30:22.412
That's what I need.

00:30:22.449 --> 00:30:24.474
I need to look inside myself...

00:30:24.518 --> 00:30:26.076
figure out
what's happening to me.

00:30:26.120 --> 00:30:27.883
I need answers.

00:30:27.921 --> 00:30:30.446
Will you help me, Commander?

00:30:31.492 --> 00:30:33.960
All right...

00:30:33.994 --> 00:30:36.189
but I want you to understand

00:30:36.230 --> 00:30:38.425
the vision quest
isn't a quick fix.

00:30:38.465 --> 00:30:40.865
It'll take time
to interpret the images

00:30:40.901 --> 00:30:41.959
and there's no guarantee

00:30:42.002 --> 00:30:43.629
you'll find
what you're looking for.

00:30:43.671 --> 00:30:45.605
I understand.

00:30:45.639 --> 00:30:47.834
What should I do to prepare?

00:30:47.875 --> 00:30:50.207
You'll need a medicine bundle.

00:30:50.244 --> 00:30:54.340
Items that define you,
things that will ground you,

00:30:54.381 --> 00:30:56.474
allow you to take the journey
into yourself.

00:30:57.518 --> 00:30:59.611
I'll get ready.

00:31:01.588 --> 00:31:04.182
This belonged to my sister,
Alixia.

00:31:04.224 --> 00:31:05.953
She made it
during our expedition

00:31:06.026 --> 00:31:07.425
to the Dunes of Talmouth.

00:31:10.731 --> 00:31:12.460
A flower from Kes's garden.

00:31:15.736 --> 00:31:19.433
And last, but not least,
the Guiding Tree.

00:31:19.473 --> 00:31:22.670
It stands at the center
of Talaxian afterlife,

00:31:22.710 --> 00:31:25.144
deep inside the Great Forest.

00:31:25.179 --> 00:31:27.443
It's there to help
us find our way

00:31:27.481 --> 00:31:28.914
when we first arrive.

00:31:28.949 --> 00:31:31.645
At least, that's what
I used to believe.

00:31:33.921 --> 00:31:36.685
Not a very impressive
medicine bundle, is it?

00:31:36.724 --> 00:31:38.214
Lt'll do fine.

00:31:38.258 --> 00:31:41.318
Now, place your hand
on the akoonah.

00:31:44.531 --> 00:31:46.158
Am I doing this right?

00:31:46.200 --> 00:31:47.929
Try to relax.

00:31:47.968 --> 00:31:51.802
Clear your mind of everything
but the objects before you.

00:31:51.839 --> 00:31:54.034
Focus on them.
Nothing else exists.

00:32:03.817 --> 00:32:06.149
Ah-koo-chee-moya.

00:32:06.186 --> 00:32:08.552
We are far
from the sacred places

00:32:08.589 --> 00:32:10.079
of our grandfathers.

00:32:10.124 --> 00:32:12.615
We are far from the bones
of our people.

00:32:12.659 --> 00:32:15.719
We come here seeking guidance.

00:32:17.197 --> 00:32:19.062
It's time, Neelix.

00:32:19.099 --> 00:32:21.567
Try to leave this room,
this ship...

00:32:21.602 --> 00:32:22.899
and go to a place
where you were

00:32:22.936 --> 00:32:25.734
the most peaceful and content
you have ever been.

00:32:25.773 --> 00:32:28.105
That's where your journey
will begin.

00:32:37.484 --> 00:32:40.180
Neelix... good to have you back.

00:32:40.220 --> 00:32:42.085
It's-it's good to be
back, Lieutenant.

00:32:47.594 --> 00:32:48.583
Alixia?

00:32:52.032 --> 00:32:55.126
Alixia, it's me, Neelix!

00:32:55.169 --> 00:32:56.295
Over here.

00:33:02.509 --> 00:33:04.670
Captain!
My sister...

00:33:04.711 --> 00:33:06.770
she was just standing here
talking to you.

00:33:06.814 --> 00:33:08.247
The dead girl.

00:33:08.282 --> 00:33:10.045
Oh, yes. Very charming.

00:33:10.083 --> 00:33:12.847
I can see
the family resemblance.

00:33:12.886 --> 00:33:14.410
Alixia!

00:33:17.624 --> 00:33:19.148
You will be assimilated.

00:33:19.193 --> 00:33:21.286
No time for that now.
Maybe later.

00:33:21.328 --> 00:33:23.296
Potent stuff.

00:33:33.640 --> 00:33:36.905
It's... It's beautiful.

00:33:36.944 --> 00:33:40.641
Yes. It's just like you
always imagined it would be.

00:33:40.681 --> 00:33:42.808
The trees, the sunlight,

00:33:42.850 --> 00:33:44.977
and all the people
who ever loved you.

00:33:45.052 --> 00:33:50.718
When I died, I looked for you,
but you weren't there.

00:33:50.757 --> 00:33:52.725
Why weren't you there?

00:33:52.759 --> 00:33:54.488
Because it's all a lie.

00:33:54.528 --> 00:33:55.825
What do you mean?

00:33:55.863 --> 00:33:59.230
You've wasted
your entire life believing lies.

00:33:59.266 --> 00:34:00.699
The "Great Forest."

00:34:00.734 --> 00:34:04.135
The "afterlife."

00:34:04.171 --> 00:34:06.639
It's all created
out of your fear of death.

00:34:06.673 --> 00:34:08.265
None of it's real.

00:34:08.308 --> 00:34:11.300
If that's true,
what's the point of living?

00:34:11.345 --> 00:34:12.505
There isn't any.

00:34:12.546 --> 00:34:16.243
That's what you're finally
starting to realize.

00:34:17.784 --> 00:34:19.843
I'm afraid to go to sleep.

00:34:19.887 --> 00:34:22.117
Tell me about the Great Forest,
Neelix.

00:34:22.155 --> 00:34:24.316
Tell me about the trees
and the grass

00:34:24.358 --> 00:34:26.656
and all the people
who loved you.

00:34:26.693 --> 00:34:28.820
Why are you saying these things?

00:34:29.997 --> 00:34:31.157
Scared you!

00:35:08.135 --> 00:35:11.571
You died on that shuttlecraft,
Neelix.

00:35:11.605 --> 00:35:13.800
They never should have
brought you back.

00:35:13.840 --> 00:35:17.276
It was a mistake
and you know it.

00:35:17.311 --> 00:35:19.142
Now accept it.

00:35:20.247 --> 00:35:21.805
You know what you have to do.

00:35:23.550 --> 00:35:24.778
No.

00:35:26.453 --> 00:35:29.286
It's all a lie.
They lied to you.

00:35:29.323 --> 00:35:31.450
You know what you have to do.

00:35:31.491 --> 00:35:34.551
We gather on this day
to tell Neelix what he must do.

00:35:34.594 --> 00:35:36.824
You stand alone.

00:35:36.863 --> 00:35:38.091
Life is irrelevant.

00:35:38.131 --> 00:35:39.496
Let go.

00:35:39.533 --> 00:35:40.761
It's pointless.

00:35:40.801 --> 00:35:42.826
It's a lie.

00:35:42.869 --> 00:35:45.861
You know what you have to do.

00:35:45.906 --> 00:35:48.397
No!

00:36:00.887 --> 00:36:02.514
Neelix.

00:36:02.555 --> 00:36:04.716
Oh, there you are.
I didn't see you.

00:36:04.757 --> 00:36:06.384
Are you looking for me?

00:36:06.426 --> 00:36:08.291
Yes, as a matter of fact, I am.

00:36:08.328 --> 00:36:09.818
I hope I'm not disturbing you.

00:36:09.862 --> 00:36:11.523
You are not.

00:36:11.564 --> 00:36:13.657
I...

00:36:13.700 --> 00:36:17.397
I want to apologize
for my outburst the other day

00:36:17.437 --> 00:36:18.404
in the Mess Hall.

00:36:18.438 --> 00:36:20.303
No apology is necessary.

00:36:20.340 --> 00:36:23.605
No. No, please,
my behavior was uncalled for.

00:36:23.643 --> 00:36:25.508
I didn't mean the things I said.

00:36:25.545 --> 00:36:26.512
I wasn't myself.

00:36:26.546 --> 00:36:29.538
But I feel much better now.

00:36:29.582 --> 00:36:31.846
Commander Chakotay
has helped me to...

00:36:31.884 --> 00:36:33.476
understand a few things.

00:36:33.519 --> 00:36:37.080
I want you to know
that I don't blame you

00:36:37.123 --> 00:36:38.317
for bringing me back.

00:36:38.358 --> 00:36:40.189
To life, I mean.

00:36:40.226 --> 00:36:42.387
In fact, what you did
was very thoughtful.

00:36:42.428 --> 00:36:44.760
I would have done the same
for any member of this crew.

00:36:44.797 --> 00:36:47.197
Yes. I'm sure you would have.

00:36:49.068 --> 00:36:51.263
Is there something else?

00:36:51.304 --> 00:36:53.238
No.

00:36:56.209 --> 00:36:57.870
Yes.

00:36:57.910 --> 00:36:59.377
Seven, I think you've made

00:36:59.412 --> 00:37:01.346
a wonderful addition
to this crew.

00:37:01.381 --> 00:37:03.542
I know it's been
difficult for you

00:37:03.583 --> 00:37:06.575
making the transition
from Borg back to human.

00:37:06.619 --> 00:37:08.052
Or half human.

00:37:08.087 --> 00:37:09.486
Or whatever it is you've become.

00:37:09.522 --> 00:37:11.353
Actually, you're
just plain Seven to me.

00:37:11.391 --> 00:37:13.325
Your point, Mr. Neelix.

00:37:13.359 --> 00:37:16.226
I guess I just want to say...

00:37:19.465 --> 00:37:22.457
you're surrounded by people
who care about you.

00:37:22.502 --> 00:37:23.764
And whether you know it or not,

00:37:23.803 --> 00:37:25.896
Voyager is going to be
a very good home to you.

00:37:25.938 --> 00:37:27.405
It certainly was to me.

00:37:27.440 --> 00:37:28.532
Was?

00:37:28.574 --> 00:37:30.132
Do you intend to leave?

00:37:31.544 --> 00:37:34.240
Leave?
No. I'll be around.

00:37:36.149 --> 00:37:37.275
Well...

00:37:39.552 --> 00:37:40.678
good-bye.

00:37:40.720 --> 00:37:42.153
Good-bye.

00:37:52.064 --> 00:37:54.259
What happened to you
this morning?

00:37:54.300 --> 00:37:57.463
I'm sorry I had to cancel
our little chat,

00:37:57.503 --> 00:37:59.937
but I was needed
in the Mess Hall.

00:37:59.972 --> 00:38:01.667
I've been so busy
the last few days

00:38:01.707 --> 00:38:04.073
I let things slip around here.

00:38:04.110 --> 00:38:06.237
You're not holding up
your end of the bargain.

00:38:06.279 --> 00:38:08.144
What do you mean?

00:38:08.181 --> 00:38:11.048
When you asked me to guide you
on a vision quest I agreed,

00:38:11.083 --> 00:38:14.052
but I also told you it was part
of an ongoing process.

00:38:14.086 --> 00:38:16.145
We're supposed to be
discussing your progress.

00:38:16.189 --> 00:38:18.555
What's left to say?

00:38:18.591 --> 00:38:19.683
I've told you...

00:38:19.725 --> 00:38:22.421
I saw my sister,
the Great Forest.

00:38:22.462 --> 00:38:24.259
I feel a sense of peace

00:38:24.297 --> 00:38:26.925
I've never felt
in my entire life.

00:38:26.999 --> 00:38:28.694
It worked.

00:38:28.734 --> 00:38:30.065
You've only lived
with the visions

00:38:30.102 --> 00:38:31.501
for a couple of days.

00:38:31.537 --> 00:38:33.664
That's not enough time
to draw any conclusions.

00:38:33.706 --> 00:38:36.573
You've got to reflect
on the images, examine them.

00:38:36.609 --> 00:38:39.100
Allow them to stay alive
in your mind.

00:38:39.145 --> 00:38:40.635
A vision quest isn't just
a dream you dismiss

00:38:40.680 --> 00:38:42.614
after your first cup of coffee.

00:38:42.648 --> 00:38:44.741
I understand.

00:38:44.784 --> 00:38:46.115
Good.

00:38:46.152 --> 00:38:48.245
I get off duty at 1400 hours.

00:38:48.287 --> 00:38:50.221
Meet me in my quarters
and we'll begin.

00:38:50.256 --> 00:38:51.587
That's an order.

00:38:51.624 --> 00:38:52.852
Yes, sir.

00:39:17.750 --> 00:39:19.047
Computer, lights off.

00:39:23.923 --> 00:39:26.187
And finally, Mr. Tuvok...

00:39:26.225 --> 00:39:30.719
I'm grateful for the opportunity
I had to win your respect.

00:39:30.763 --> 00:39:33.926
Your strength and your wisdom
were an inspiration to me

00:39:33.966 --> 00:39:37.026
and I can only hope
that your memory of me

00:39:37.069 --> 00:39:39.936
will serve to inspire you
in some way.

00:39:41.507 --> 00:39:45.739
It was an honor to spend my last
years on Voyager with this crew.

00:39:45.778 --> 00:39:47.268
I want to thank all of you

00:39:47.313 --> 00:39:49.372
for your kindness
and companionship.

00:39:49.415 --> 00:39:51.383
Good-bye.

00:39:53.419 --> 00:39:55.284
Computer, end log
and code for delivery

00:39:55.321 --> 00:39:56.913
to Captain Janeway in one hour.

00:40:13.805 --> 00:40:15.272
Captain, someone's trying
to initiate

00:40:15.307 --> 00:40:17.707
an unauthorized transport.

00:40:17.743 --> 00:40:18.937
It's Neelix.

00:40:18.977 --> 00:40:20.444
Where's he going?

00:40:20.479 --> 00:40:22.606
Looks like he's trying
to beam into the nebula.

00:40:23.649 --> 00:40:24.638
Stop him.

00:40:26.051 --> 00:40:27.541
Janeway to Neelix.

00:40:27.586 --> 00:40:28.951
Neelix, respond.

00:40:28.987 --> 00:40:32.150
Neelix, I order you
to disengage transport.

00:40:36.728 --> 00:40:38.719
He's found a way
to block the abort sequence.

00:40:38.764 --> 00:40:40.163
Transport's in progress.

00:40:40.198 --> 00:40:41.722
Override it! Get him back.

00:40:51.810 --> 00:40:53.107
Bridge to Chakotay.

00:40:53.145 --> 00:40:55.545
We've blocked
his transporter signal.

00:40:55.580 --> 00:40:57.309
You can slow me down,
but you can't stop me.

00:40:57.349 --> 00:40:59.544
What are you trying to do?

00:40:59.584 --> 00:41:01.017
I'm going back where I belong.

00:41:01.053 --> 00:41:02.247
You belong here, Neelix.

00:41:02.287 --> 00:41:03.549
Not anymore.

00:41:03.588 --> 00:41:04.782
I died in that nebula.

00:41:04.823 --> 00:41:06.051
You should've left me.

00:41:06.091 --> 00:41:07.581
- Neelix...
- No closer!

00:41:07.626 --> 00:41:09.457
I've created
a site-to-site transport.

00:41:09.494 --> 00:41:11.052
No one can override the signal.

00:41:11.096 --> 00:41:13.257
You told me you were at peace.

00:41:13.298 --> 00:41:17.098
I will be...
as soon as I tap this control.

00:41:17.135 --> 00:41:19.069
What really happened
in your vision quest?

00:41:19.104 --> 00:41:20.833
What did you see?

00:41:24.943 --> 00:41:28.401
My sister, the crew, myself.

00:41:28.447 --> 00:41:31.245
They all told me
the same thing...

00:41:31.283 --> 00:41:34.218
there's no point in living,
and I agree with them.

00:41:34.252 --> 00:41:36.220
I'm sure
those were powerful images,

00:41:36.254 --> 00:41:38.222
but there are many ways
to interpret them.

00:41:38.256 --> 00:41:40.986
You may be coming face-to-face
with your own fear of death.

00:41:41.093 --> 00:41:43.618
Or the manifestation
of your emotional crisis.

00:41:43.662 --> 00:41:46.256
Your deepest beliefs
have been thrown into doubt.

00:41:46.298 --> 00:41:48.960
It's only natural the vision
quest would reflect that.

00:41:49.001 --> 00:41:54.064
11 years ago,
I saw my world in ruins...

00:41:56.174 --> 00:41:58.665
my family murdered.

00:41:58.710 --> 00:42:00.143
All that's kept me going

00:42:00.178 --> 00:42:03.079
is knowing that one day
we'd be together again.

00:42:04.483 --> 00:42:06.212
That I'd see them again.

00:42:09.054 --> 00:42:11.318
But it's not true.

00:42:11.356 --> 00:42:14.223
And I can't...
live without that hope.

00:42:14.259 --> 00:42:15.248
I understand how this

00:42:15.293 --> 00:42:17.261
can change
the way you look at things,

00:42:17.295 --> 00:42:20.128
but it can also lead
to an even stronger faith.

00:42:20.165 --> 00:42:21.894
You don't know.

00:42:21.933 --> 00:42:23.423
You're not there yet.

00:42:23.468 --> 00:42:25.129
Ensign Wildman to Neelix.

00:42:26.805 --> 00:42:28.067
Answer her!

00:42:28.106 --> 00:42:30.768
Neelix, please respond.

00:42:33.945 --> 00:42:35.310
No.

00:42:35.347 --> 00:42:37.747
You're being called
back to your life again, Neelix.

00:42:37.783 --> 00:42:39.683
Don't turn your back on it.

00:42:39.718 --> 00:42:41.948
We're your family now.

00:42:43.822 --> 00:42:45.119
It's not enough.

00:42:45.157 --> 00:42:46.454
It is for us.

00:42:46.491 --> 00:42:48.686
"His function on this crew
is diverse."

00:42:48.727 --> 00:42:50.490
That's what Seven of Nine
said about you.

00:42:50.529 --> 00:42:52.759
Even our Borg understands
how important

00:42:52.798 --> 00:42:54.663
you are on this ship.

00:42:54.699 --> 00:42:56.667
It's not just the duties
you perform.

00:42:56.701 --> 00:42:59.431
It's the way you make
people feel when you're around.

00:43:01.106 --> 00:43:02.937
That Neelix is gone.

00:43:03.008 --> 00:43:05.533
I don't think he is.

00:43:05.577 --> 00:43:07.545
Why didn't you answer me?

00:43:07.579 --> 00:43:10.139
I had to have the computer
track you down.

00:43:10.182 --> 00:43:13.049
Naomi thought she saw
a monster in the replicator.

00:43:15.620 --> 00:43:17.520
Neelix, what's going on?

00:43:22.294 --> 00:43:24.956
I'm trying to decide
some things.

00:43:25.063 --> 00:43:27.054
That little girl
needs you, Neelix.

00:43:28.633 --> 00:43:30.828
Monsters in the replicator?

00:43:30.869 --> 00:43:33.167
Who else on this ship
can handle that?

00:43:59.831 --> 00:44:01.526
Duty calls.

00:44:15.380 --> 00:44:16.347
Good night, sir.

00:44:16.381 --> 00:44:17.643
He says good night.

00:44:21.186 --> 00:44:22.813
Good night, Naomi.

00:44:22.854 --> 00:44:23.912
Good night.

00:44:27.292 --> 00:44:28.691
What's the matter?

00:44:28.727 --> 00:44:30.888
Mommy says you were sick.

00:44:30.929 --> 00:44:34.262
I was, but I'm okay now.

00:44:34.299 --> 00:44:36.096
Did a monster get you?

00:44:38.303 --> 00:44:41.101
Yes, I suppose so.

00:44:41.139 --> 00:44:43.767
But I chased him away.

00:44:45.677 --> 00:44:46.974
Pleasant dreams.
